+    <section id="primary-mask-lookup-contract"><h2>Primary-mask lookup fitting contract</h2><p>BUG-058 primary_cache_mask consumes A=cached value, B=preserve mask and Y=primary_preserve_table; returns A=B=combined mask and stores the original value in OBJ_VALUE. The caller CMPA replaces condition flags before use. render_entity_colour initializes Y once; the positive-mode entity loop and replay preserve it, and IRQ restores it. The 52-byte immutable table indexes only value AND $33 (maximum 51); no new mutable state is allocated. Rebind and full-cache replay do not use this lookup. Source-adjacent audit declarations link the constant table to its pointer load; exhaustive runtime byte tests establish index semantics beyond the lexical audit.</p></section><section id="contract-composition">
       <h2>How to read a contract</h2>
       <p>Each routine contract is the combination of its unique purpose below and one named interface profile. The profile supplies inputs, outputs, conservative clobbers, memory reads, memory writes, side effects, and invariants. A narrower source-local header overrides the conservative register set but may not widen memory ownership or weaken an invariant. Generated module pages add current callers, callees, source lines, addresses, and emitted bytes; they do not own semantic meaning.</p>
       <p>In each routine table, <strong>label</strong> is the authored global symbol and stable link target, <strong>purpose</strong> is that routine's owned operation, <strong>profile</strong> selects the complete interface contract, and <strong>coverage reason</strong> states why fail-closed documentation requires the routine.</p>
